<rml>
<head>
	<title>System Menu</title>
	<link type="text/rcss" href="base.rcss"/>
	<link type="text/rcss" href="sys_menu.rcss"/>
</head>
<body>
	<!-- Modern theme's own copy of the system menu -- per-theme file (UI::RmlBridge::
	     LoadThemedDocument) because modern-frame/modern-frame-crimson is genuinely modern-specific
	     structure, not just style -- the shared ../../sys_menu.rml is legacy's own theme-neutral
	     copy and carries neither (a "shared" file must not bake in one theme's vocabulary, same
	     reasoning login.rml/msg_win.rml/remember_password_prompt.rml/my_inventory.rml/
	     my_quest_info.rml already forked for). .panel-cap-top/.panel-middle/.panel-cap-bottom stay
	     in the markup (SysMenuWin.cpp binds nothing to them directly) but render as nothing under
	     modern -- this theme's own base.rcss/sys_menu.rcss declare no matching rule for them,
	     unlike legacy's real sprite-backed versions. Keep this file's ids/data-model/event-callback
	     names in sync with ../../sys_menu.rml -- SysMenuWin.cpp binds against both by the same
	     names. -->
	<div id="backdrop"></div>
	<div id="panel" class="center-both modern-frame modern-frame-crimson" data-class-compact="select_server_hidden" data-model="sys_menu">
		<div id="panel_middle" class="panel-middle"></div>
		<div class="panel-cap-top"></div>
		<div class="panel-cap-bottom"></div>
		<div id="btn_exit_game" class="btn" data-event-click="sysmenu_exit_game_click">{{exit_game_label}}</div>
		<div id="btn_select_server" class="btn" data-class-hidden="select_server_hidden" data-event-click="sysmenu_select_server_click">{{select_server_label}}</div>
		<div id="btn_option" class="btn" data-event-click="sysmenu_option_click">{{option_label}}</div>
		<div id="btn_close" class="btn" data-event-click="sysmenu_close_click">{{close_label}}</div>
	</div>
</body>
</rml>
